Dialogue: 1,0:00:00.10,0:00:05.20,Name,,0,0,0,,{\pos(88,1298)\fad(120,120)}Ashley Dalton MP
Dialogue: 1,0:00:00.10,0:00:05.20,Party,,0,0,0,,{\pos(88,1376)\fad(120,120)}Labour · West Lancashire
Dialogue: 2,0:00:00.00,0:00:05.08,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}I was overwhelmed with\Ngrief, fear and anxiety;
Dialogue: 2,0:00:05.08,0:00:07.44,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}I was scared of\Nwhat was to come,
Dialogue: 2,0:00:07.44,0:00:08.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}and fearful of how\Nit would impact
Dialogue: 2,0:00:08.90,0:00:10.92,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}my family and my loved ones.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:10.92,0:00:12.08,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}I was scared that\NI was going to
Dialogue: 2,0:00:12.08,0:00:15.36,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}get really poorly and\Nthinking, "How will I cope?
Dialogue: 2,0:00:15.36,0:00:17.02,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}How will my family cope?
Dialogue: 2,0:00:17.02,0:00:18.42,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}How will I be cared for?
Dialogue: 2,0:00:18.42,0:00:20.04,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}How will I afford it?
Dialogue: 2,0:00:20.04,0:00:21.96,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}How badly will it hurt?
Dialogue: 2,0:00:21.96,0:00:25.66,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}How long will it last?"\NWhen you hear those words,
Dialogue: 2,0:00:25.66,0:00:30.54,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}depression, anxiety,\Ngrief, fear,
Dialogue: 2,0:00:30.54,0:00:34.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}shame and guilt\Ncome in bounds.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:35.24,0:00:39.72,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}Suicide risk is highest\Nimmediately after diagnosis,
Dialogue: 2,0:00:39.72,0:00:43.56,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}and it usually falls quickly,\Nwithin three to six months.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:43.56,0:00:46.46,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}I would be lying\Nif I said that when
Dialogue: 2,0:00:46.46,0:00:48.56,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}thinking about all\Nthat was to come,
Dialogue: 2,0:00:48.56,0:00:51.38,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}I did not consider\Nthat it might be fairer
Dialogue: 2,0:00:51.38,0:00:54.22,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}and easier on everyone\Nif I just got the
Dialogue: 2,0:00:54.22,0:00:56.67,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}dying over with as\Nsoon as possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.82,0:01:01.92,Shape,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(60,1290)\1c&HF48542&\bord0\shad0\fad(120,120)\p1}m 0 0 l 617 0 l 617 78 l 0 78{\p0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.82,0:01:01.92,Shape,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(60,1368)\1c&H242120&\bord0\shad0\fad(120,120)\p1}m 0 0 l 617 0 l 617 60 l 0 60{\p0}
Dialogue: 1,0:00:56.82,0:01:01.92,Name,,0,0,0,,{\pos(88,1298)\fad(120,120)}Carla Lockhart MP
Dialogue: 1,0:00:56.82,0:01:01.92,Party,,0,0,0,,{\pos(88,1376)\fad(120,120)}DUP · Upper Bann
Dialogue: 2,0:00:56.72,0:00:58.82,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}The soft language of "assisted
Dialogue: 2,0:00:58.82,0:01:01.50,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}dying" is misleading\Nthe public,
Dialogue: 2,0:01:01.50,0:01:05.58,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}because it obscures\Nthe stark and very dark
Dialogue: 2,0:01:05.58,0:01:09.46,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}reality of what is\Nactually being proposed.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:09.46,0:01:11.54,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}We should always\Nhave the courage
Dialogue: 2,0:01:11.54,0:01:14.66,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}to call things what they are.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:14.66,0:01:17.88,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}Of course, we all want\Nassistance when we are dying,
Dialogue: 2,0:01:17.88,0:01:18.34,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}but that is not what\Nthis Bill provides.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:18.34,0:01:18.64,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}It is not about\Nan extra shot of
Dialogue: 2,0:01:18.34,0:01:18.64,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}morphine to ease\Nsomeone on their way;
Dialogue: 2,0:01:18.34,0:01:18.64,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}it is a Bill that allows\Ndoctors to provide
Dialogue: 2,0:01:18.34,0:01:18.64,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}lethal drugs for a\Npatient to end their life.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:18.34,0:01:18.64,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}Let the reality of that\Nsink in: our great NHS,
Dialogue: 2,0:01:18.34,0:01:18.64,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}the principles of which are\Nto protect and to save lives,
Dialogue: 2,0:01:18.34,0:01:18.64,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}would be responsible for\Nstate-sponsored suicide.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:18.34,0:01:21.42,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}That is what it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.22,0:01:52.32,Shape,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(60,1290)\1c&HF48542&\bord0\shad0\fad(120,120)\p1}m 0 0 l 552 0 l 552 78 l 0 78{\p0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.22,0:01:52.32,Shape,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(60,1368)\1c&H242120&\bord0\shad0\fad(120,120)\p1}m 0 0 l 552 0 l 552 60 l 0 60{\p0}
Dialogue: 1,0:01:47.22,0:01:52.32,Name,,0,0,0,,{\pos(88,1298)\fad(120,120)}Janet Daby MP
Dialogue: 1,0:01:47.22,0:01:52.32,Party,,0,0,0,,{\pos(88,1376)\fad(120,120)}Labour · Lewisham East
Dialogue: 2,0:01:47.12,0:01:49.76,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}I previously voted\Nfor assisted dying.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:49.76,0:01:51.58,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}I recognised\Nthen, as I do now,
Dialogue: 2,0:01:51.58,0:01:53.70,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}the deep turmoil that\Nfamily members experience
Dialogue: 2,0:01:53.70,0:01:55.02,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}when they know that their\Nloved ones are dying,
Dialogue: 2,0:01:55.02,0:01:57.76,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}or see them die.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:57.76,0:02:00.14,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}The agonising distress\Nor pain that they
Dialogue: 2,0:02:00.14,0:02:02.40,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}experience is something\Nthat no one wants
Dialogue: 2,0:02:02.40,0:02:05.26,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}for themselves or\Ntheir loved ones.
Dialogue: 2,0:02:05.26,0:02:05.72,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}However,
Dialogue: 2,0:02:05.72,0:02:08.64,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}I cannot shake from my\Nmind a conversation I had
Dialogue: 2,0:02:08.64,0:02:12.60,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}with someone some time\Nago about assisted dying.
Dialogue: 2,0:02:12.60,0:02:16.64,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}They had been diagnosed\Nwith HIV/AIDS before the
Dialogue: 2,0:02:16.64,0:02:19.68,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}time of advanced medication\Nfor this illness.
Dialogue: 2,0:02:19.68,0:02:20.88,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}Their body was breaking down,
Dialogue: 2,0:02:20.88,0:02:22.06,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}and they had been\Ninformed that
Dialogue: 2,0:02:22.06,0:02:24.32,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}their prognosis was bleak.
Dialogue: 2,0:02:24.32,0:02:26.04,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}They said that\Nhad assisted dying
Dialogue: 2,0:02:26.04,0:02:29.42,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}been an option for them then,\Nthey would have taken it.
Dialogue: 2,0:02:29.42,0:02:32.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}However, it was not an option,
Dialogue: 2,0:02:32.00,0:02:33.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}and they have since\Nbeen stabilised on
Dialogue: 2,0:02:33.90,0:02:36.75,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}medication and are\Nin full-time work.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.90,0:02:42.00,Shape,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(60,1290)\1c&HF48542&\bord0\shad0\fad(120,120)\p1}m 0 0 l 617 0 l 617 78 l 0 78{\p0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.90,0:02:42.00,Shape,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(60,1368)\1c&H242120&\bord0\shad0\fad(120,120)\p1}m 0 0 l 617 0 l 617 60 l 0 60{\p0}
Dialogue: 1,0:02:36.90,0:02:42.00,Name,,0,0,0,,{\pos(88,1298)\fad(120,120)}Ms Julie Minns MP
Dialogue: 1,0:02:36.90,0:02:42.00,Party,,0,0,0,,{\pos(88,1376)\fad(120,120)}Labour · Carlisle
Dialogue: 2,0:02:36.80,0:02:39.76,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}As a relative who\Nsaw the inadequacy of
Dialogue: 2,0:02:39.76,0:02:43.12,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}social care eat away\Nat the self-respect
Dialogue: 2,0:02:43.12,0:02:45.36,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}of a once fiercely\Nindependent woman,
Dialogue: 2,0:02:45.36,0:02:47.80,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}leaving her to\Nconclude that she was a
Dialogue: 2,0:02:47.80,0:02:50.30,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}burden and would\Nbe better off dead,
Dialogue: 2,0:02:50.30,0:02:54.92,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}I know that access\Nto every possible
Dialogue: 2,0:02:57.44,0:02:57.74,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}form of support was\Nnot there for her.
Dialogue: 2,0:02:57.44,0:03:00.58,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}As the daughter who sat\Nat a hospital bedside,
Dialogue: 2,0:03:00.58,0:03:02.02,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}having agreed to\Nthe withdrawal
Dialogue: 2,0:03:02.02,0:03:03.74,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}of invasive treatment,
Dialogue: 2,0:03:03.74,0:03:06.96,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}only to watch my\Nsemi-conscious mother scream
Dialogue: 2,0:03:06.96,0:03:10.56,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}for water that was wrongly\Nwithheld and writhe
Dialogue: 2,0:03:10.56,0:03:13.76,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}in agony because specialist\Npalliative care was
Dialogue: 2,0:03:13.76,0:03:17.98,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}only available nine to\Nfive on Monday to Friday,
Dialogue: 2,0:03:17.98,0:03:21.52,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}I know that access\Nto every form
Dialogue: 2,0:03:21.52,0:03:24.75,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}of support was\Nnot there for her.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.90,0:03:30.00,Shape,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(60,1290)\1c&HF48542&\bord0\shad0\fad(120,120)\p1}m 0 0 l 888 0 l 888 78 l 0 78{\p0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.90,0:03:30.00,Shape,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(60,1368)\1c&H242120&\bord0\shad0\fad(120,120)\p1}m 0 0 l 888 0 l 888 60 l 0 60{\p0}
Dialogue: 1,0:03:24.90,0:03:30.00,Name,,0,0,0,,{\pos(88,1298)\fad(120,120)}Sir Bernard Jenkin MP
Dialogue: 1,0:03:24.90,0:03:30.00,Party,,0,0,0,,{\pos(88,1376)\fad(120,120)}Conservative · Harwich and North Essex
Dialogue: 2,0:03:24.80,0:03:28.06,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}Maybe there should be\Na citizens assembly
Dialogue: 2,0:03:28.06,0:03:30.32,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}on this question—it\Nis a subject that
Dialogue: 2,0:03:30.32,0:03:32.28,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}would lend itself to\Na citizens assembly.
Dialogue: 2,0:03:32.28,0:03:33.20,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}[Interruption.] Well,
Dialogue: 2,0:03:33.20,0:03:36.24,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}it would not take away\Nany power from this House.
Dialogue: 2,0:03:36.24,0:03:38.86,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}This House would still\Nbe able to decide,
Dialogue: 2,0:03:38.86,0:03:40.88,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}but it would inform\Nthe debate in a way
Dialogue: 2,0:03:40.88,0:03:44.68,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}that the debate is\Nstill not informed.
Dialogue: 2,0:03:47.48,0:03:51.18,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}My mother and father passed\Naway in recent years,
Dialogue: 2,0:03:51.18,0:03:53.86,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}and I am so grateful\Nthat my mother
Dialogue: 2,0:03:53.86,0:03:56.64,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}never had to confront\Nthis question.
Dialogue: 2,0:03:56.64,0:03:59.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}She often said, “Oh,\NI just want to die.
Dialogue: 2,0:03:59.00,0:04:04.20,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}I am just a burden on\Nthe family.” Though she
Dialogue: 2,0:04:04.20,0:04:05.48,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}would never have\Nqualified for this Bill,
Dialogue: 2,0:04:05.48,0:04:07.82,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}I am so grateful\Nthat there were never
Dialogue: 2,0:04:07.82,0:04:09.96,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}any circumstances\Nthat would possibly
Dialogue: 2,0:04:09.96,0:04:11.99,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}have confronted her\Nwith this question.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.14,0:04:17.24,Shape,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(60,1290)\1c&HF48542&\bord0\shad0\fad(120,120)\p1}m 0 0 l 888 0 l 888 78 l 0 78{\p0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.14,0:04:17.24,Shape,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(60,1368)\1c&H242120&\bord0\shad0\fad(120,120)\p1}m 0 0 l 888 0 l 888 60 l 0 60{\p0}
Dialogue: 1,0:04:12.14,0:04:17.24,Name,,0,0,0,,{\pos(88,1298)\fad(120,120)}Dame Karen Bradley MP
Dialogue: 1,0:04:12.14,0:04:17.24,Party,,0,0,0,,{\pos(88,1376)\fad(120,120)}Conservative · Staffordshire Moorlands
Dialogue: 2,0:04:12.04,0:04:14.18,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}I say to colleagues who\Nsupported the Bill before
Dialogue: 2,0:04:14.18,0:04:17.60,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}and have wrestled sincerely\Nwith the issue since:
Dialogue: 2,0:04:17.60,0:04:19.36,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}you do not have to\Nrepudiate the vote you
Dialogue: 2,0:04:19.36,0:04:22.24,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}cast last time to vote\Ndifferently today.
Dialogue: 2,0:04:22.24,0:04:23.86,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}You do not have to decide that
Dialogue: 2,0:04:23.86,0:04:26.28,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}assisted dying can\Nnever be right.
Dialogue: 2,0:04:26.28,0:04:28.08,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}You do not have to\Nabandon the compassion
Dialogue: 2,0:04:28.08,0:04:30.60,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}that led you to\Nsupport the principle.
Dialogue: 2,0:04:30.60,0:04:33.94,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}You need only ask whether\Nthis Bill, in this form,
Dialogue: 2,0:04:33.94,0:04:35.88,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}on the evidence\Nbefore us today,
Dialogue: 2,0:04:35.88,0:04:40.26,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}is safe enough for Parliament\Nto force it into law.
Dialogue: 2,0:04:40.26,0:04:41.74,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}That is today's test.
Dialogue: 2,0:04:41.74,0:04:42.04,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}There is no shame whatsoever\Nin concluding that
Dialogue: 2,0:04:41.74,0:04:43.04,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}the answer to a different\Nquestion is different.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.46,0:04:53.56,Shape,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(60,1290)\1c&HF48542&\bord0\shad0\fad(120,120)\p1}m 0 0 l 888 0 l 888 78 l 0 78{\p0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.46,0:04:53.56,Shape,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(60,1368)\1c&H242120&\bord0\shad0\fad(120,120)\p1}m 0 0 l 888 0 l 888 60 l 0 60{\p0}
Dialogue: 1,0:04:48.46,0:04:53.56,Name,,0,0,0,,{\pos(88,1298)\fad(120,120)}Dr Ben Spencer MP
Dialogue: 1,0:04:48.46,0:04:53.56,Party,,0,0,0,,{\pos(88,1376)\fad(120,120)}Conservative · Runnymede and Weybridge
Dialogue: 2,0:04:48.36,0:04:50.44,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}As a former mental health\Ndoctor and someone who
Dialogue: 2,0:04:50.44,0:04:52.60,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}has done research on\Ndecision-making capacity,
Dialogue: 2,0:04:52.60,0:04:55.40,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}I want to talk about stigma in\Nthe brief time I have today.
Dialogue: 2,0:04:55.60,0:04:59.08,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}I have looked after many\Nhundreds of people—perhaps
Dialogue: 2,0:04:59.08,0:05:03.42,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}thousands—who have self-harmed\Nor attempted suicide.
Dialogue: 2,0:05:03.42,0:05:03.74,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}Of course,
Dialogue: 2,0:05:03.74,0:05:07.02,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}a desire for one's life\Nto end can be entirely
Dialogue: 2,0:05:07.02,0:05:09.68,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}reasonable and an\Nunderstandable wish,
Dialogue: 2,0:05:09.68,0:05:11.58,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}but it is often\Na manifestation
Dialogue: 2,0:05:11.58,0:05:14.50,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}of a treatable\Nmental disorder.
Dialogue: 2,0:05:16.26,0:05:18.82,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}With the right intervention,\Ncare and support,
Dialogue: 2,0:05:18.82,0:05:20.48,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}people can get better.
Dialogue: 2,0:05:20.48,0:05:23.60,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}They can look back and\Nsay, "What was that about?
Dialogue: 2,0:05:23.60,0:05:25.70,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}I'm so thankful I\Ndidn't succeed" when
Dialogue: 2,0:05:25.70,0:05:28.34,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}they get the care and\Ntreatment they need.
Dialogue: 2,0:05:28.48,0:05:30.87,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1600)}The Bill refuses to\Nacknowledge that.
